1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Every model you download is code you did not write. This is Quarantine — an offline clean room that runs it where it cannot hurt you.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:19,000
First, the scanner everyone already runs. Picklescan reports zero infected files and zero suspicious globals. It is clean, and it is wrong.

3
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:30,000
That is the gap. Neither picklescan nor fickling ever opens a Python file, and seven of our nine malicious artifacts hide in exactly those files.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:39,000
So we execute it inside Docker, with the network off, a read-only root, every capability dropped, and an audit hook recording every sensitive operation.

5
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:48,000
The artifact runs, and the trace shows what it did: a file read outside its own directory, and a DNS lookup to an address that cannot resolve.

6
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:59,000
This is behaviour, not a signature. The artifact cannot rename its way out of it, and the trace is the evidence everything downstream reasons over.

7
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Then an agent team reads it. The analyst decides and cites trace ids. The challenger tries to refute it. The repairer rewrites the offending function, and a verifier proves it.

8
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:29,000
And when we cannot look, we escalate. This artifact could not be executed, so its code path was never observed: UNKNOWN, exit code two, a human decides.

9
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:46,000
We also ran picklescan's own malicious corpus — ninety-one samples, one per real advisory. They flag eighty-eight; we observe forty-three. They win there, and we say so. This is the other half of the pair, not a replacement.

10
00:01:46,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Then we pointed it at Nepal: two hundred and sixty-eight repositories, forty-six shipping Python, fifteen requiring remote code. That search found a bug in our own tool.

11
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:17,000
The measured numbers. Nine of nine on our labeled corpus, against two of nine for each incumbent. Zero false positives on twenty real published models, where fickling flags eighteen.

12
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:32,000
The repair is proven, not asserted — identical outputs on twelve prompts and zero capability operations, measured from the trace. Six of seven verified, and the seventh is a refusal we state plainly.

13
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:44,000
We attacked our own box: ten breakout primitives, including host mounts and runtime sockets. Zero succeeded. That is a measurement, not a guarantee.

14
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:55,000
And here is what we do not claim. No scanner bypass, no proof the box cannot be broken, poisoned weights out of scope, and the corpus is ours.

15
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:02,000
Quarantine. Apache two. No API key, no egress, and receipts you can verify with openssl. Thank you.
